  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;1) N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;2) N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;3) N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;4) Refer to Notes to Financial Statements, Page 122, Note 6.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;5) N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;padding-left:12pt"&gt;Organization and Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Marketlink, LLC (Marketlink or the Company), is a Delaware limited liability company and a wholly owned subsidiary of South Bow Infrastructure Inc. Marketlink offers crude oil transportation services from Cushing, Oklahoma to the United States (U.S.) Gulf Coast. To provide these transportation services, Marketlink leases pipeline capacity from South Bow (USA) LP and has constructed ancillary interconnection facilities at Cushing, including tanks and metering facilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Marketlink&#8217;s activities are subject to regulation by various authorities including, but not limited to, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as construction, operations, rates and ratemaking, and agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;padding-left:12pt"&gt;Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The financial statements of the Company are prepared in accordance with accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the U.S. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;In preparing these financial statements, Marketlink is required to make estimates and assumptions that affect both the amount and timing of recording assets, liabilities, revenues and expenses since the determination of these items may be dependent on future events. The Company uses the most current information available and exercises careful judgment in making these estimates. In the opinion of management, these financial statements have been properly prepared within reasonable limits of materiality and conform in all material respects to the Uniform System of Accounts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Carrier Property&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:3pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Carrier property is carried at cost. Depreciation is calculated on a straight-line basis once the assets are ready for their intended use. Carrier property is depreciated at various rates that have been filed with and accepted by the FERC. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Revenue &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:3pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company&#8217;s revenues are generated from contractual arrangements for committed capacity and from the transportation of crude oil, under a tariff regulated by the FERC, as well as from providing crude oil storage services. Revenues earned from contracted capacity arrangements are recognized ratably over the term of the contract regardless of the amount of crude oil that is transported. Revenues for volumetric-based services are recognized when the service is performed. The Company does not take ownership of the crude oil that it transports for customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Income Tax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company is not subject to federal or state income tax. The income tax effect of the Company&#8217;s activities accrues to its parent and has accordingly not been recorded in the Company&#8217;s financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;padding-left:12pt"&gt;Taxes Payable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Taxes payable consists of pipeline property taxes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;padding-left:12pt"&gt;Affiliated Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Operating and Administrative Services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;At June 30, 2026, South Bow Infrastructure Holdings Ltd. (a wholly-owned subsidiary of South Bow PipeLines Limited (SB PipeLines)), through wholly-owned subsidiaries, was responsible for developing and operating the Company&#8217;s facilities. Marketlink was charged by SB PipeLines and its wholly-owned subsidiaries for services provided.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Pipeline Capacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:3pt;padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Marketlink has leased pipeline capacity on South Bow (USA) LP&#8217;s system from Cushing, Oklahoma to the U.S. Gulf Coast (Gulf Coast Leg) to provide crude oil transportation services. Marketlink&#8217;s lease payments to South Bow (USA) LP are calculated based on its proportional share of the Gulf Coast Leg&#8217;s total capacity and cost of service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;At June 30, 2026, South Bow Marketing USA Ltd. (SBMU), a wholly owned subsidiary of South Bow USA Infrastructure Holdings LLC. (South Bow USA), had agreements for pipeline and storage capacity with Marketlink. SBMU also transports uncommitted volumes on Marketlink.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Cash Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;At June 30, 2026, a cash management agreement was in place between Marketlink and South Bow USA, a wholly-owned subsidiary of South Bow Infrastructure Holdings Ltd. Monies advanced under the agreement were considered to be a loan, accruing interest and repayable on demand. Marketlink received interest on monies advanced to South bow USA at the rate of interest earned by South Bow USA on its short-term cash investments. Marketlink paid interest on monies advanced from South Bow USA based on South Bow USA&#8217;s short-term borrowing costs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;padding-left:12pt"&gt;Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;At June 30, 2026, the Company had no commitments. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%;padding-left:12pt"&gt;Legal Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company is from time to time subject to litigation incidental to its business. The Company is not aware of any contingent liabilities that would have a material adverse effect on the Company&#8217;s financial condition, results from operations, or cash flows. The Company is not aware of any material contingent liabilities with respect to compliance with applicable environmental laws and regulations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
